<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25131" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭtōnē</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ithōnē</span></b> ), ēs,
			f., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Itōnus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city and mountain in
				Bœotia</i> (or <i>Thessaly</i>), <i>with a temple of Pallas</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 2,
				720</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cat. 64,
			228</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> ‡
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ito-nida</span></b>  (an error for
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Itōnis</span></b> ),
				Minerva a loco sic appeliata, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				105</span></i> Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭtōnaei</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ithōn-</span></b> ), ōrum,
			m., <i>the inhabilants of Itone</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 7,
				330</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭtōnĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰτώνιος,</span>
			<i>Itonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templum Minervae Itoniae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					36, 20, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
